The viewer compiles hpgl.c, chardraw.c, clip.c, fillpoly.c, pendef.c and lindef.c.
The adapter redirects stdio to bounded memory streams and contains exit recovery
inside C. patch.cmake applies checked edits only to the extracted build copy:
numeric/label/polygon bounds, typed failures, per-call state and explicit reset
style records. No raster backend, command-line program or external font library
is included. The SVG serializer consumes the native intermediate records.

Initial supported scope: first-page HPGL vectors, curves, built-in ASCII labels,
standard line patterns and upstream polygon fills; normal HPGL ESC envelopes.
User-defined UL patterns use upstream expansion, bounded to 19 elements and
indices 1..8, with nonnegative lengths and a positive total. UL resets work.
Encoded PE polylines, AD/SD font selection, unavailable
glyph/centering tables, non-ASCII labels, parameterized BP plot metadata, custom
CR color ranges, FP nonzero-winding fills and PT fill-pen thickness currently
return unsupported. Bare BP, default CR, NP256, MC0 and TR0 are accepted.
This is not a general PCL renderer.
Unrecognized commands return unsupported rather than a partial success.
Known upstream geometry fidelity limitations still require corpus comparison.
